{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZrpr43j9dq3MY1S9QApvm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tdef min_operations_to_rearrange(n: int, s: str, t: str) -> int:\n2\t    \"\"\" Given two strings s and t of length n consisting of 'B' and 'W' characters,\n3\t    determine the minimum number of operations needed to transform the initial configuration s\n4\t    into the target configuration t.\n5\t    \n6\t    Initially, there are n stones placed in cells 1 to n according to string s,\n7\t    where 'W' represents a white stone and 'B' represents a black stone.\n8\t    There are also two empty cells at positions n+1 and n+2.\n9\t    \n10\t    In one operation, you can:\n11\t    - Choose two adjacent cells that both contain stones\n12\t    - Move these two stones to the two empty cells while preserving their order\n13\t    \n14\t    Return the minimum number of operations needed to achieve configuration t,\n15\t    or -1 if it's impossible.\n16\t    \n17\t    Args:\n18\t        n: Number of stones (2 <= n <= 14)\n19\t        s: Initial configuration string of length n\n20\t        t: Target configuration string of length n\n21\t    \n22\t    Returns:\n23\t        Minimum number of operations, or -1 if impossible\n24\t    \n25\t    >>> min_operations_to_rearrange(6, 'BWBWBW', 'WWWBBB')\n26\t    4\n27\t    >>> min_operations_to_rearrange(6, 'BBBBBB', 'WWWWWW')\n28\t    -1\n29\t    >>> min_operations_to_rearrange(3, 'BBW', 'BBW')\n30\t    0\n31\t    \"\"\"\n32\t    raise NotImplementedError\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"517beed7-d66d-4de9-95f8-4b25e1fd706a","uuid":"62531111-7f2f-48b2-8f40-841f16ff1561","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:50:15.655Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/pg-runs/baseline-v3-wsl-sonnet55-low_lcb-oneoff-12-rep1/solution.py","content":"def min_operations_to_rearrange(n: int, s: str, t: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\" Given two strings s and t of length n consisting of 'B' and 'W' characters,\n    determine the minimum number of operations needed to transform the initial configuration s\n    into the target configuration t.\n    \n    Initially, there are n stones placed in cells 1 to n according to string s,\n    where 'W' represents a white stone and 'B' represents a black stone.\n    There are also two empty cells at positions n+1 and n+2.\n    \n    In one operation, you can:\n    - Choose two adjacent cells that both contain stones\n    - Move these two stones to the two empty cells while preserving their order\n    \n    Return the minimum number of operations needed to achieve configuration t,\n    or -1 if it's impossible.\n    \n    Args:\n        n: Number of stones (2 <= n <= 14)\n        s: Initial configuration string of length n\n        t: Target configuration string of length n\n    \n    Returns:\n        Minimum number of operations, or -1 if impossible\n    \n    >>> min_operations_to_rearrange(6, 'BWBWBW', 'WWWBBB')\n    4\n    >>> min_operations_to_rearrange(6, 'BBBBBB', 'WWWWWW')\n    -1\n    >>> min_operations_to_rearrange(3, 'BBW', 'BBW')\n    0\n    \"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HZrpr43j9dq3MY1S9QApvm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
